# Arc's File ▸ New Easel (⌃⇧E, Arc 1.172.1, docs/arc-parity.md "Easels, measured"): a Today tab on an
# easel:// address whose page is Cra's canvas, not a web page; it comes back after a relaunch.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://action/newEasel
wait 2
cra://debug?browserWindows=created
expect-log Cra browser windows created: kind=normal .*tabs=\[easel://[0-9A-F-]{36}\] open=easel://[0-9A-F-]{36} page=1
relaunch
wait 4
cra://debug?browserWindows=relaunched
expect-log browser windows relaunched: kind=normal listed=1 tabs=1 open=1
cra://action/viewEasels
wait 1
# Arc's tile under the pointer (Arc 1.173.1, recorded 17 Nov 2026): it grows by 6 % about its
# centre and its backing brightens, in a tenth of a second, and goes back when the pointer leaves.
cra://debug?easelTileHover=1
expect-log easel tile: hover=on scale=1\.060 fill=0\.08 title=Untitled Easel
cra://debug?easelTileHover=0
expect-log easel tile: hover=off scale=1\.000 fill=0\.04 title=Untitled Easel
# The capture menu's New Easel: an easel with the capture on it opens in a new tab (after the
# relaunch only cra.log is read, which counts tabs rather than naming them).
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=captured
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://debug?captureToEasel=1
wait 2
cra://debug?browserWindows=captured
expect-log browser windows captured: kind=normal listed=1 tabs=3 open=1
# Send To… an easel: the capture lands on the easel edited last, next to the first one.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=sent
wait 2
cra://debug?captureToEasel=send
expect-log capture sent to an easel, which now holds 2 items
# The easel was open in a tab: the capture shows on its canvas and is in its file. (It was written
# to the file behind the canvas, which then saved what it had shown before over it.)
wait 1
cra://debug?easels=open
expect-log easel open: shown=2 saved=2 title=Untitled Easel
# Captures keep the page they came from (Arc's WebCard) and can show it live: a page of its own,
# laid out at the captured size, drawn onto the card about once a second.
cra://debug?easelLive=5
expect-log easel capture: host=127\.0\.0\.1 viewport=[0-9]+x[0-9]+ area=[0-9]+x[0-9]+@0,0 canGoLive=true
wait 6
expect-log easel live: frames=[1-9][0-9]* image=[0-9]+x[0-9]+
# A pasted web address is a link card with the page's title (Arc's LinkData).
cra://debug?easelLink=${PAGE}?n=linked
wait 4
expect-log easel link: host=127\.0\.0\.1 title=
# Arc 1.172.2's shapes, colour picker and object menu, on a new easel.
cra://action/newEasel
wait 2
cra://debug?easelDraw=1
cra://debug?easelPick=0
expect-log easel pick: picker=shown color=lightGreen menu=Bring to Front\|Send to Back\|Delete\|—\|Cut\|Copy\|Paste\|—\|Duplicate$
# Arc 1.173.1's tool keys and the toolbar under the pointer: R picks the rectangle and its
# letter shows in the button's corner; the pointer over another tool shows that one's too; Escape
# goes back to the pointer, whose button has no letter; Duplicate shows none either.
cra://debug?easelTool=r
expect-log easel toolbar: picked=rectangle hover=none letters=r$
cra://debug?easelTool=-&hover=freehand
expect-log easel toolbar: picked=rectangle hover=freehand letters=r,p$
cra://debug?easelTool=esc&hover=duplicate
expect-log easel toolbar: picked=pointer hover=duplicate letters=$
cra://debug?easelTool=o&hover=none
expect-log easel toolbar: picked=ellipse hover=none letters=o$
cra://debug?easelTool=v
expect-log easel toolbar: picked=pointer hover=none letters=$
# promise: #580
# The canvas has no edge (Cra's own; Arc's is a fixed width that grows down): it opens on the home
# sheet's top left with a view's room on every side, scrolling far past Arc's 2436 pt or up and left
# of the home sheet still finds room, and View ▸ Zoom Out and Actual Size zoom it about the view's middle
# (opening, the view's top may sit under the title bar's inset).
cra://debug?easelCanvas=-
expect-log easel canvas: zoom=1\.00 view=0,(0|-[0-9]+),[0-9]+,[0-9]+ extent=-[0-9]+,-[0-9]+,[0-9]+,[0-9]+ room=yes$
cra://debug?easelCanvas=3000,9000
expect-log easel canvas: zoom=1\.00 view=3000,9000,[0-9]+,[0-9]+ extent=.* room=yes$
cra://debug?easelCanvas=-4000,-3000
expect-log easel canvas: zoom=1\.00 view=-4000,-3000,[0-9]+,[0-9]+ extent=.* room=yes$
cra://action/zoomOut
cra://debug?easelCanvas=-
expect-log easel canvas: zoom=0\.91 view=-40[0-9][0-9],-30[0-9][0-9],[0-9]+,[0-9]+ extent=.* room=yes$
cra://action/resetZoom
cra://debug?easelCanvas=-
expect-log easel canvas: zoom=1\.00 view=-400[0-2],-300[0-2],[0-9]+,[0-9]+ extent=.* room=yes$
# Arc 1.173.1's capture menu: a Send To… field that has the keyboard, the capture's actions,
# Retake, then New Easel and every easel by name. Typing narrows the rows, and a row is where the
# capture goes: New Easel makes one with it, an easel's row puts it on that easel.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=menu
wait 2
cra://debug?captureMenu=-
expect-log capture menu: typed= keyboard=field rows=Copy\|Save\.\.\.\|Send via iMessage\.\.\.\|—\|Retake\|—\|New Easel\|Untitled Easel\|Untitled Easel\|Untitled Easel$
cra://debug?captureMenu=new&run=New Easel
expect-log capture menu: typed=new keyboard=field rows=New Easel$
wait 2
cra://debug?easels=open
expect-log easel open: shown=1 saved=1 title=Untitled Easel
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=menu2
wait 2
cra://debug?captureMenu=untitled&run=Untitled Easel
expect-log capture menu: typed=untitled keyboard=field rows=Untitled Easel\|Untitled Easel\|Untitled Easel\|Untitled Easel$
wait 2
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=menu3
wait 2
cra://debug?captureMenu=untitled&run=Untitled Easel
expect-log capture sent to an easel, which now holds 3 items
# Library ▸ Easels follows an easel made while it shows (it used to wait for a tab to close).
cra://action/viewEasels
wait 1
cra://debug?easels=tiles
expect-log easel tiles: 4$
cra://action/newEasel
wait 2
cra://debug?easels=tiles
expect-log easel tiles: 5$
